{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Laminus \u2014 OrcaSlicer Sidecar API (API v1)",
    "description": "Headless 3D model slicing via OrcaSlicer CLI running inside a Docker container. Laminus is a sidecar service used by Themis; it is not intended to be called directly by end-users in normal operation.\n\n## Typical agent workflow\n\n1. **`GET /api/health`** \u2014 wait until `catalog_loaded: true` before making any other calls.\n2. **`GET /api/profiles`** \u2014 discover machine / process / filament UUIDs for your printer and material. Filter by `manufacturer`, `model`, and `nozzle` to narrow results.\n3. **`POST /api/slice/start`** \u2014 upload the model (`.3mf` or `.stl`) with the resolved UUIDs. The response contains a `job_id`.\n4. **`GET /api/slice/status/{job_id}`** \u2014 poll every 2\u20135 s until `status` is `completed` or `failed`.\n5. **`GET /api/slice/download/{job_id}`** \u2014 retrieve the GCode (or `.3mf` when `export_3mf` was requested). Downloading evicts the job immediately.\n\nAlternatively, use **`POST /api/slice/prepared`** when the 3MF already embeds print settings from a previous OrcaSlicer session \u2014 no profile resolution is needed.\n\n## Packing / arrangement\n\nUse **`POST /api/pack`** to distribute STL geometry across build plates before slicing. Three modes: supply a template `.3mf`, profile UUIDs (preferred \u2014 catalog-aware), or explicit bed dimensions. The packed `.3mf` is returned directly (synchronous, up to 120 s).\n\n## Error conventions\n\n- **422** \u2014 caller-side validation failure (bad UUIDs, missing required fields, etc.).\n- **503** \u2014 Laminus is not yet ready; the catalog is still building. Retry after `GET /api/health` reports `catalog_loaded: true`.\n- **400 / 408 / 500** \u2014 OrcaSlicer-side failures; check server logs for details.",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
